WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.303
This is agnt: your coding agent's eyes and hands in a real browser.

00:00:05.303 --> 00:00:11.974
One bug report, taken from diagnosis to full end-to-end coverage — through the floating proxy UI.

00:00:08.750 --> 00:00:16.752
The developer reports the bug in the floating panel — it goes straight over the proxy's channel to the agent, which picks it up and answers in the same overlay.

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:23.945
The agent runs layout diagnostics through the proxy.

00:00:23.945 --> 00:00:32.082
Five issues, each outlined on the page: the root cause is a translate-Z-zero hack creating a containing block that traps the pinned note.

00:00:32.082 --> 00:00:34.750
The CSS audit grades the damage.

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:41.472
The diagnosis becomes a site-wide regression check — red, five violations.

00:00:41.472 --> 00:00:44.922
The agent applies the fix, and the check runs green.

00:00:44.922 --> 00:00:51.436
And the fix holds: the export menu renders in full and takes clicks, and the note finally answers.

00:00:54.070 --> 00:00:56.099
Finally, the dynamic form.

00:00:56.099 --> 00:01:06.051
The agent drives every failure condition end to end: a passing baseline, empty required fields, an invalid email, seats out of range.

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:25.256
Then the server-side failures: a duplicate company rejected with 409, a plan rule violation at 422, and a raw 500 surfaced to the user.

00:01:25.256 --> 00:01:31.386
Six failure-condition tests and one green baseline — generated, observed, and verified.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:34.081
agnt.

00:01:34.081 --> 00:01:35.775
Give your agent the browser.

